WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.306 --> 00:00:04.809
- [Narrator] This is
Wesley, a Patagonian mara.

00:00:04.809 --> 00:00:07.862
He looks like a cross
between a deer and a rabbit,

00:00:07.862 --> 00:00:11.017
but Wesley is actually a rodent.

00:00:11.017 --> 00:00:14.341
Patagonian maras are only
found in parts of central

00:00:14.341 --> 00:00:16.022
and south Argentina,

00:00:16.022 --> 00:00:19.751
and even there they are
becoming harder to spot.

00:00:19.751 --> 00:00:23.268
These cute little guys top
out at just under three feet,

00:00:23.268 --> 00:00:25.620
and just over 30 pounds.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.734
Their bodies are well adapted for running,

00:00:27.734 --> 00:00:32.632
and they reach close to 45
miles per hour at full speed.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:36.361
Grass makes up the majority
of this herbivore's diet.

00:00:36.361 --> 00:00:38.867
They prefer living in areas
with lots of shrub cover

00:00:38.867 --> 00:00:41.976
to protect themselves from predators.

00:00:41.976 --> 00:00:45.257
However, a combination of
overgrazing and hunting

00:00:45.257 --> 00:00:47.800
for their skin has caused a steady decline

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.005
in their population.

00:00:50.005 --> 00:00:52.338
This is the Patagonian mara.

